%% figure
%% owner: the maintainer (README, Feedback)
%% source: docs/diagrams/federated-flow.mermaid (this file). Export: federated-flow.svg (docs/diagrams/exports.json)
%% question: In what order do the public operations run for one verification-grade message between two entities on different providers, from resolution to verification years later?
%% profile: 2 (four-corner); one grade (verification), the default scope, one message
%% status: current
%% references: docs/federated-flow-explainer.md (the phase-by-phase walkthrough); I-D "Message Flows and Delivery States"; TS clauses 4.1 and 6; wallet-rdp-openapi.yaml; delivery-service-openapi.yaml; rdp-relay-openapi.yaml; docs/adr/SBM-ADR-0015.md (one provider role); docs/REVIEW_AGENDA.md A1, A10
%% alt: Seven phases. Resolution and discovery at the directory and the recipient's provider. First contact: the sender reserves and commits KeyPackages, creates the group, deposits one Welcome per device and registers as the group's founder; each recipient device collects its Welcome and acknowledges it, which is joining, or refuses it with a typed outcome the creator collects. Submission to RDP(out), which obtains its Delivery Service's acceptance of the same octets before sealing the SE. RDP-to-RDP relay of the octets with the SE; RDP(in) checks them and forwards them to its Delivery Service with the origin proven, then returns B.1 or B.2. Delivery: the device collects and acknowledges, and the Delivery Service signs the S2 receipt; no published operation carries it to an RDP (open, A1). The recipient's confirmation reaches RDP(in), which issues the DE, or on a verified mismatch or at expiry the NDE. RDP(out) composes the Evidence Package. Later verification decodes each artefact, verifies seals and timestamps and checks admission at each act's instant.
%% end figure
%% SBM — full four-corner federated flow: verification-grade message between
%% two entities on different providers, from name resolution to evidence
%% verification. Informative; the normative flow is in
%% ietf/draft-sbm-mls-erd-00.md (Message Flows and Delivery States) and
%% etsi/TS-SBM-QERDS-Binding-v0.1.md (clauses 4.1, 6). Actors S=sender side,
%% R=recipient side.
%%
%% The relay is RDP-to-RDP and carries the ciphertext WITH the SE (an
%% relay between two transport providers was drawn here before and was never published); RDP(in)
%% forwards to its DS with the origin proven by that SE; the join is the
%% Welcome acknowledgement; the creator is routed as the group's founder;
%% live admission is a lease. An earlier edition of this figure taught a
%% superseded protocol and was replaced.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor WS as WU-S · Sender wallet (Entity A)
    participant EDD as EDD · Directory
    participant MO as DS(out) · RDP(out)'s
    participant RO as RDP(out) · QERDS
    participant RI as RDP(in) · QERDS
    participant MI as DS(in) · RDP(in)'s
    actor WR as WU-R · Recipient wallet (Entity B)

    Note over WS,WR: Phase 1 — Resolution & discovery
    WS->>EDD: resolve(UID-B)
    EDD-->>WS: DirectoryRecord (status, med_url, pinned seal keys) — sealed
    WS->>MI: GET BW-MED / BW-ORG / BW-MEMBER
    MI-->>WS: sealed documents — verified against the pinned keys (LINT-TRUST-05)

    Note over WS,WR: Phase 2 — First contact (MLS group, E2EE)
    WS->>MI: reserve KeyPackages for B's devices (Idempotency-Key)
    MI-->>WS: reservation + keypackage_ref per device (RFC 9420 RefHash)
    WS->>MI: commit reservation — packages CONSUMED from here
    WS->>WS: create group (A+B devices), pin sbm_group_params, Commit
    WS->>MI: deposit one Welcome per device (+ group_info_commitment)
    WS->>MI: register as the group's founder · device-authenticated — MLS adds no Welcome for its creator
    WR->>MI: collect WelcomeQueue (Welcome + commitment + offered_suite)
    WR->>WR: decrypt Welcome, recompute GroupInfo commitment, verify credentials
    alt commitment matches, suite ≥ floor
        WR->>WR: join group
        WR->>MI: acknowledge (DELETE /welcome/{welcome_id}) — joining: the routing claim outlives the Welcome's expiry
    else mismatch / suite below floor
        WR->>MI: refuse (POST /welcome/{welcome_id}/refusal · group-info-mismatch / suite-below-published-floor)
        MI-->>WS: creator collects the typed outcome (GET /group-establishment/outcomes)
    end

    Note over WS,WR: Phase 3 — Submit (content stays E2E encrypted)
    WS->>WS: build envelope, payload_hash, encrypt · SIGN the submission tuple (sender_confirmation)
    WS->>RO: submit(exact MLSMessage octets + metadata) · authenticated member session
    RO->>RO: validate request, identity, expiry, policy, sender signature — before anything moves
    RO->>MO: POST /messages (the SAME octets) · RDP credential
    MO->>MO: accept — digest computed HERE · items only for devices it observed joining (here: none)
    MO-->>RO: AcceptanceRecord (binds octets, issuing RDP, message_id)
    RO-->>WS: SE (A.1-SubmissionAcceptance) — sealed + qualified timestamp, AFTER acceptance

    Note over RO,MI: Phase 4 — Four-corner relay (RDP-to-RDP: ciphertext + SE)
    Note over RO,RI: peer-RDP auth: Trusted List + register<br/>admission: a LEASE decided at the exchange's start<br/>— not evidence of admission at any act
    RO->>RI: POST /relay/messages — the SAME octets + the sealed SE
    RI->>RI: verify the SE's seal · SHA-256(octets) == the SE's envelope_hash, or refuse the hop
    RI->>MI: POST /messages as forwarder · origin = RDP(out) + its sealed SE
    MI->>MI: origin proven by the SE · keyed (RDP(out), message_id) · one item per device it observed joining (B's, and the founder)
    MI-->>RI: AcceptanceRecord — issuing_rdp_id RDP(out), forwarding_rdp_id RDP(in)
    RI-->>RO: POST /relay/messages/{message_id}/result — B.1 RelayAcceptance (or B.2), sealed + QTS at this hop

    Note over WS,WR: Phase 5 — Deliver & decrypt (S1 → S2 → S3)
    WR->>MI: collect (device-authenticated) → transferred + collection token
    WR->>MI: acknowledge (receipt-ack, collection token)
    MI-->>WR: DeliveryReceipt — DS-signed, server-observed instant = S2
    Note over MI,RI: OPEN (agenda A1): the DE issuer MUST verify this receipt, and no published operation delivers it to any RDP
    WR->>WR: decrypt, recompute payload_hash

    alt digest matches (S3)
        WR->>RI: confirmation s3 (wallet-signed or member-bound session)
        RI->>RI: verify signer · roster (active ack-capable member) · tuple == SE
        RI->>RI: evaluate acceptance_policy — S4 when the completing member's confirmation arrives (any-one ⇒ S4 == S3)
        RI-->>WR: DE — delivered_at = when RDP(in) verified the completing confirmation, never the S2 receipt · embeds s3_attestation
    else digest mismatch
        WR->>RI: confirmation mismatch — the recipient's signed proof
        RI-->>RO: NDE (D.2, payload-hash-mismatch) — carries that proof
    else no confirmation before expiry
        RI-->>RO: NDE (expired) — silence is never a mismatch
    end

    Note over WS,WR: Phase 6 — Evidence Package
    RO->>RO: compose EP: se + outcome + rdp_chain[RDP(out), RDP(in)] — sealed + QTS
    Note over RO: composing is an act: RDP(out) admitted at the EP's own QTS instant
    RO-->>WS: EP (wallet-storable)
    RI-->>WR: EP / DE (wallet-storable)

    Note over WS,WR: Phase 7 — Verification (later, by any relying party)
    WR->>WR: decode artefact [COSE_Sign1, QTS] · verify seal over dCBOR(body) · QTS imprints SHA-256(seal)
    WR->>WR: validate decoded body against its JSON Schema (authoritative) · payload_hash == held plaintext
    WR->>WR: admission of every provider at its act's instant (authenticated register) · QSealC → Trusted Lists (production)
    Note over WS,WR: qualification and admission are independent gates — neither implies the other
